1. The Booster T2's proportions and joint ranges

   The humanoid's proportions, the order and ranges of its leg joints, and
   the ranges of its arm joints up to the elbow come from the T2 model that
   Booster Robotics publishes (BoosterRobotics/booster_assets,
   robots/T2/T2_31dof_JZgripper). Its segment masses are used as a check on
   ours. None of its meshes is in this tree.

   Where: src/pluggybot/humanoid/model.py, and the files it writes,
   models/humanoid.xml and models/humanoid.json.
   License: BSD 3-Clause License, Copyright (c) 2025, BoosterRobotics.
   The full text is in models/booster_assets.LICENSE.

2. AprilTag markers

   The marker images in models/tags/ and protocol/textures/ are markers of
   the tag36h11 family from the AprilTag library. The moms-apriltag package
   drew them.

   AprilTag: BSD 2-Clause License, Copyright (C) 2013-2015, The Regents of
   The University of Michigan. The full text is in models/apriltag.LICENSE.
   moms-apriltag: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 Kevin J. Walchko. The full
   text is in models/moms_apriltag.LICENSE.

